    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, can you help me with a depreciation calc? I have a piece of equipment that cost $45,000. It has an estimated salvage value of $5,000 and a useful life of 8 years. I need to find the annual straight-line depreciation amount. Can you walk me through the steps?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To calculate the annual straight-line depreciation, you first need to find the depreciable cost, which is the cost minus the salvage value. Then, you divide that depreciable cost by the useful life of the asset. For your equipment, the calculation is: $(\\$45,000 - \\$5,000) / 8 \\text{ years}$. This results in an annual depreciation of $\\$5,000$.",
      "source": "target",
